   "title": "Dettato \u2014 Audio to MIDI",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Dettato \u2014 Audio to MIDI\n\nMulti-instrument transcription with [KobiMusic's dettato](https://github.com/kobimusic/dettato): one track per instrument (73 classes) plus a drum track.\n\n**Loader**\n- `model`: `dettato` downloads the stage weights into `models/dettato` on first use (~113 MB total). A folder in that directory holding any stage subfolder is read from disk instead.\n- Chain the Evidence / Grouper / Drums nodes after the Loader to enable a stage; a node that is not in the graph is bypassed and its weights are never downloaded.\n\n**Transcribe**\n- Takes any `AUDIO` (Load Audio, or a video's audio track).\n- Drums only run on sources recorded at 40 kHz or more.\n- `min_velocity` drops quiet notes.\n- `dedup` (off here) drops redundant tracks when several sources share an instrument name; for separated stems it would keep only the stem with the most notes of it.\n- The output is performance MIDI; if you want the notes to sit on the grid, run the `midi` output through a **Dettato Quantize MIDI** node (not in this graph) with the song's `tempo` and `grid`.\n\n**Output**\n- Piano Roll node: one lane per track, drums in the lower panel (px_per_ms / max_seconds / show_drum_panel to tweak).\n- MIDI: one General MIDI track per instrument, named after it. The JSON summary is the info_json output of the Transcribe node (save it with a text node when needed).\n- Notes are performance MIDI (not beat-quantized)."
   ]
  },
